Day 4. - Level 20.
---------------------

"You hear a guard patrolling the area".

Ok.. does that mean that there should be a treasure trove
somewhere? (Trevor trove? Spinal tap.. legends) I've got an idea... I'll 
drink my potion of object detection! Ahha! There it is, a square group 
of $'s. Pulled out my wand of digging and got busy.. woohoo, an extra 
$5000 to donate to someone.. and...

"You activated a magic portal!"
"You feel dizzy for a moment, then the sensation passes"
"You penetrated a high securiy area! An alarm sounds"

Wahhey, I'm in Fort Ludios - for only the second time ever! It's a pity 
that I can't turn on tiles because I remember it looking quite pretty. 
Oh well have to use my imagination. (Let's just hope it won't look like 
Itchy and Scratchy just standing there).

Fortunately I picked up an amulet of ESP - now I can see whats on the 
other side of that wall. As I'm using ASCII mode, I still really don't 
have it ingrained what half of the characters stand for. I'm going to be 
using the ; key quite a lot for the next 30 minutes! The only enemy that 
I'm worried about are ones that could cast a spell and crumble my armour 
- from what I know only Liches or Silver Naga's could do that. None so 
far, so let's go.

What's their problem? I didn't ask to invade their castle. I didn't want 
to kill everyone.

An interesting thing just happened, a winter wolf cub threw a blast of 
frost at me and I got this:

"The blast of frost hits you!"
"But it reflects from your armour!"

Ahha, I have reflection! Yes. There's nothing worse than being decimated 
by a death ray or a sleep ray.. it's happened to me enough times.

A ring of conflict would be really useful right about now.

Hmm, bad news. A succubus has appeared and asked me to take off most of 
my armour. Of course I said "no" whenever I could resist, but it looks 
like on Fort Ludios you can't teleport. So the succubus kept on sleeping 
with me about 5 times in a row. Well that's not the bad news. In the 
meantime a Xorn appeared through the wall and started chomping on me 
before I got a chance to dress again! HP down to 46! Time for a quick 
escape! Jump into the teleport!

So I've come back out onto level 20. Let's rest for a bit and get my HP 
back up. Ok, great, back to full strength and with full armour, let's go 
kill that Xorn! Jump in the teleport.. and boy was I angry. The Xorn 
went down in two strokes. The rest of the monsters decided to start 
pouring through the door.. 20 kills later, I managed to kill and eat a 
wraith corpse, to take me up to level 14, enough to do my quest! Woohoo.

Also found a wand of make invisible and zapped myself with it. Cool. I 
wonder if that will fool the soldiers? Ahha.. looks like it. The battle 
royale begins...

"the seargeant hits you with a chickatrice corpse"

WHHAHATT?? Since when did the enemy know to do that? It's not something 
that _I've_ ever had the guts to do!

"you are slowing down"

Hmm. Only two options left. Pray (a sure cure if I am safe to pray, 
which I __shoould__ be, I hope), or
use my unicorn horn. (Not sure if that works)

#pray

"you begin praying to Crom"

"You feel that Crom is well-pleased.  You feel more limber."

WHEW!!

Ok ok, holy crap. Some idiot soldier is swinging around an almost 
"insta-death" weapon. And if I kill him, couldn't another soldier try to 
do the same thing? Only if he's wearing gloves I guess... it's still 
pretty scary. Timeout time.

There's actually a cockatrice corpse two squares away. I'm wearing 
fencing gloves. I guess I could always fight fire with fire. Or maybe 
not. I think I might do the standard nethack fighting technique, the one 
that got me to where I am today.

Run away!

On the way back to the teleport, I found a flesh golum corpse. Don't 
those guys give away intrinsics? Let's eat it and find out.

"Ulch - that meat was tainted!  You feel deathly sick."

Damn it! Talk about stupid! And I can't pray!

I might have to use the unicorn horn. It's not blessed, but that's as 
good as I've got.

apply unicorn horn

"What a relief!"

Yay!!

Ok. That was a couple of very stupid moves. I think I might go to my 
quest level and try to complete it. Sounds a bit safer than Fort Ludios 
for the mo.

 From level 20, back up to lvl 19.

"The blast of disintegration whizzes by you!"

Oh what????

There's a black dragon there trying to disintegrate me! (Daffy: "Lucky I 
have my disintegration gun with me.. Well what do you know, it 
disintegrated" - classic) I wonder if my reflection will protect me from 
it. Or (more excitedly), I wonder if I can eat the soon-to-be-dead 
dragon and gain disintegration resistance? Well I know one thing, at 
least I now know how to spell disintegration!

Hows this for a plan? I bugger off upstairs, wait until I'm hungry (or 
almost hungry), go back downstairs, kill the dragon and eat! Let's see 
if it works out that way...

Oh what?? I've moved a couple of squares and the dragon has changed to a 
different monster. Turns out it was a boring chemeleon. Do I gain 
polymorph control if I eat a chameleon corpse? Let's try it (I'm feeling 
dangerous).

Whoops, I'm a dragon! Well, I should have guessed. Eating a chameleon 
corpse just polymorphs you. Makes sense. And it looks like I've only 
lost my cloak in process. That's cool. Hey I wonder if dragons have 
"turn to stone resistance"? I wonder if that's such a thing?

Cool it clockwise.

Ok, so I'm a silver dragon. Ahha! I do bite! Mental note, don't go near 
any chickatrices or cockatrices!

Venture back up to level 14 and back to my homestown. How to cross the 
river without being drowned by an eel? Use my frost breath to freeze the 
water, of course!

So I fought my way down a level when I came across a teleport trap.. and 
it took me down to "Home 4" - bizarre! I thought about fighting my way 
back up so that I have a clear path to go back... but where's the fun in 
that? So I've fought my way down to Thoth Amon's level.. but stuff it, 
I'm going to bed. Next post, my battle with Thoth!

